# docs/ is ignored wholesale, EXCEPT docs/remediation/ — the remediation
# programme's decision records must stay visible to `git add`. They were
# silently invisible under the old blanket `/docs/` rule, and that already cost
# a real miss: a document was written, never staged, and nobody noticed.
#
# Only remediation/ is negated. Everything else under docs/ — including
# docs/superpowers/plans and specs, which are managed by explicit `git add -f`
# — stays ignored, so `git add` is not flooded with ~50 unrelated documents.
#
# A directory cannot be re-included while its parent is excluded, so the parent
# is excluded one level down (/docs/*) rather than wholesale (/docs/).
/docs/*
!/docs/remediation/
/venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.idea/

# Runtime artifacts
src/logs/
artifacts/llm_failures/
artifacts/log_monitor/v3_iter*.jsonl
artifacts/log_monitor/v3_live_*.jsonl
artifacts/log_monitor/extraction_v3_smoke_*.json

# Sample documents — keep out of repo
documents/

# Session-generated analysis / specs — kept offline only, not part of repo
artifacts/extraction_analysis/
artifacts/log_monitor/*.md
src/docs/model_tuning/phi4_humanization_plan.md

# Test-dataset snapshots: multi-hundred-MB pg_dump files, reproducible from a build
backups/testdata/

# Agent context/response captures written by models/context_trainer. These hold
# content lifted from customer documents; artifacts/llm_failures/ above is
# ignored for the same reason and this one was not, so 517 files sat untracked
# and one `git add .` from the remote. Aged out by services/capture_retention.
data/conversations/
backups/neo4j/

# Supervised KG rebuild transcripts (scripts/kg_full_rebuild.py)
logs/kg_rebuild*.log

# Runtime logs. logs/ held five finetune transcripts that were committed and
# then never touched again; src/logs/ is already ignored above and had grown a
# 175MB procwise.log. A log is a thing you read once and rotate, not a thing
# you version.
logs/*.log

# Outputs of the opportunity miner. api/routers/opportunities.py reads the JSON
# back on /opportunities/sync, so these DO exist at the repo root in production
# -- they are just not something to version. Both were tracked, so every
# production run dirtied the working tree with a regenerated artifact.
/opportunity_findings.json
/opportunity_findings.xlsx
